<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>synergy-team-meeting-2026-10-12</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<style>:root{color-scheme:light only;supported-color-schemes:light}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#F1F3F4">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#F1F3F4" style="background-color:#F1F3F4">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:24px 16px">
<!--[if mso]><table role="presentation" width="640" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td><![endif]-->
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="width:100%;max-width:640px;background-color:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E3E6E8;border-radius:16px">
<tr><td style="padding:32px 32px 32px 24px">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 0 0"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td style="border-left:3px solid #2E4A66;padding:0 0 0 16px"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Synergy Team Meeting: Clean Meeting Notes</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Date: Monday, October 12, 2026<br>Participants: Nasir Shaikh, Abaiyaz Zarif, Labiba Khalid, Salman Hossain, Shad Hassan. Harsh was on the invite but is not heard in the recording.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#FBF4E2" style="background-color:#FBF4E2;border-left:3px solid #8A6414;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:16px"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;color:#1B1F23">Note: These are cleaned and condensed notes, not a word-for-word transcript. Product names are corrected where the recording garbled them.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">1. VaporLock</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Product: VaporLock is a concrete additive installed at batching plants. It cuts curing time from about 90 days to about 20, and the buildings last longer. Only three companies worldwide offer a solution to this problem.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Business model: VaporLock belongs to our partner, Greg. We hold exclusive territories: Alaska, all of Mexico, and half of Northern California. A customer from outside a territory has to come through Synergy Building Technologies (SBT). Nasir has also asked Greg about Bangladesh and Pakistan.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Target audience: Engineers, planners, big builders and developers.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Marketing approach<br>Flyers are co-branded with SBT and VaporLock, and link to VaporLock’s official website.<br>Our contact details and new VaporLock emails go on every flyer. If someone contacts VaporLock corporate from our territory, the lead comes back to us.<br>Salman joins the VaporLock strategy meetings.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Actions<br>Nasir: Ask Harsh to create the two VaporLock emails (@synergybanc.com and @SynergyBuildingTech.com) and share the credentials with Abaiyaz. Share the VaporLock website login with Abaiyaz. Add Salman to VaporLock partner meetings.<br>Abaiyaz: Pull media from the VaporLock site and revamp the flyer with the SBT and VaporLock logos, the VaporLock URL, and the new emails.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">2. Ecomist and the Fertilizer Opportunity</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Background: Nasir used Claude to build a brief and newsletter from the J.P. Morgan research on how the Iran conflict affects fertilizer. Fertilizer, energy and water costs are all rising, and Ecomist helps customers use less fertilizer and less water. Nasir called it “a perfect storm” and the right moment to build attention for the product, including with banks.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Decisions<br>It is a newsletter, not a website revamp. It does not go into Lovable or onto a subdomain. Abaiyaz builds it.<br>The version to build is the HTML page with the “Go to the action plan” button and five decisions, each linking to the exact Ecomist website page. Nasir will email the exact link so nobody builds the wrong version.<br>Colors can change as long as they blend with Ecomist’s.<br>Sequence: Abaiyaz finishes the newsletter, then the team reviews the Ecomist website, then reads the brief. The whole team reviews it next week.<br>Ecomist has been licensed for a while with our Florida partners. Social replies will come in once marketing starts, and we’ll build a simple reply process.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Website updates<br>Replace the AI-looking images with real ones (no rush) and add case studies.<br>The SmartValve page is almost empty. The old Canva video is good but needs the SBT logo. Abaiyaz will rebrand it and source new media from the manufacturer’s site (founder: Tony).<br>This is time-sensitive. There is a presentation next week with a car wash owner who has about 100 gas stations. If the first site works, the others follow.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Actions<br>Nasir: Email Abaiyaz and Shad the task with the artifact link.<br>Abaiyaz: Build and test the HTML brief, replace the AI images, and update the SmartValve page.<br>Everyone: Read the Ecomist site, then the brief.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">3. Zerithon and GroundVex Creatives</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Zerithon<br>Labiba presented updated creatives. The key message is that Zerithon ionically bonds to concrete and becomes part of it, so there are no cold joints. A cold joint is where an overlay fails to fuse with the concrete beneath it.<br>Changes: add “Concrete repair technology” near the top, add “No cold joints” under the bonding message, and move “return” next to “1-hour service.”<br>The gas station photos are real images from Harsh, lightly enhanced.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Video plan<br>We’ll visit a friend’s gas station in California to film. The owner can’t close the station (a closure would cost roughly $40,000 to $50,000), so we plan to repair one small section without shutting down. If that goes well, he’ll activate his other stations.<br>Shoot both vertical video (for social reels) and horizontal video (for LinkedIn and other uses), so Labiba can cut shorter clips.<br>Nasir will send Abaiyaz an existing Zerithon explainer clip. Abaiyaz will add an AI voiceover. If it works, Nasir will make more.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">GroundVex: The updates (playground, field and pool) are done and the posts are scheduled.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Actions<br>Labiba: Update the Zerithon creatives.<br>Nasir: Schedule the site visit (owner to be confirmed) and send the clip to Abaiyaz.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">4. Social Media, Leads and Roles<br>Labiba owns posting and has everything scheduled, including newsletters.<br>Salman handles DMs, follow-ups and CRM entry. He has access to the Synergy Financial Instagram so no lead is missed.<br>Seven leads have come in through the refinance and purchase form. Nasir will review them today.<br>Newsletter posts are already generating inbound interest.<br>Nasir’s message: keep posting, and keep suggesting other places to post, such as Alignable.<br>The social dashboard is not connected yet. Shad will connect it so Claude can pull stats.<br>QuickBooks and inventory will be handled in a separate session this week.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">5. AI Tools<br>Claude: Best for connected, agentic work such as websites, databases, and linking Canva and email. Everyone should be set up by the end of the week.<br>ChatGPT: Best for high-volume marketing content and images. The current plan costs $8 per month, and we’ll upgrade if credits run out.<br>We expect to use Claude for most work and ChatGPT for a smaller share, mainly images.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">6. Landing Pages and Platform Updates (Shad)<br>The three Lovable landing pages (CoolRoof ROI, Contractor Growth, Brand Builder) are now visible in the shared workspace. Lovable’s default view shows “Recently viewed,” so open My Projects to see everything.<br>Shad is finishing the pages. Nasir will review them in Lovable once Shad confirms.<br>Shad found a way to track Lovable projects and prompts and connect them to the Command Center.<br>Coming this week: an artifact library and a thread-based module in the Command Center.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">7. Company Protocol: Communicating on Deadlines<br>Nasir’s deadlines are tied to his other commitments, so a missed date delays everything downstream. The new rule for everyone:<br>If you can’t meet a due date or can’t figure something out, say so early. Saying no is better than letting it quietly slip.<br>Nasir or Abaiyaz will then take it over, solve it, and bring it back to the team.<br>Protocols are sent to the whole team. They are company-wide rules and are not aimed at any one person.<br>Example: Nasir will find a basic Craigslist auto-posting tool, share it with Shad and Salman to test, and use it until Shad finds a better one.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 16px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Action Items by Owner<br>Nasir: Send the Ecomist newsletter task email with the artifact link. Request the VaporLock emails and share the VaporLock login. Add Salman to VaporLock meetings. Schedule the California gas station visit. Send the Zerithon clip to Abaiyaz. Review the 7 leads. Find and share a Craigslist posting tool.<br>Abaiyaz: Build and test the Ecomist HTML brief. Replace the AI images on the Ecomist site. Rebrand the SmartValve video and brochures for the car wash presentation. Create the VaporLock flyer and emails. Add the AI voiceover to the Zerithon clip. Schedule the QuickBooks inventory session.<br>Labiba: Update the Zerithon creatives and keep posting.<br>Salman: Manage DMs, follow-ups and CRM entries.<br>Shad: Finish the three Lovable landing pages and send links to Nasir. Connect the social dashboard to Claude. Build the artifact library and Command Center thread module.<br>Everyone: Get set up on Claude by the end of the week. Read the Ecomist site and brief before next week’s review. Flag early if you can’t meet a deadline.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:0"><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:32px;color:#1B1F23;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">Still to confirm<br>The new landing page deadline (the original 4 pm on Oct 12 has passed).<br>Who owns the California site visit, and the date.</p></td></tr></table></td></tr></table></td></tr>
</table>
</td></tr>
</table>
<!--[if mso]></td></tr></table><![endif]-->
</td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
